# Finding existing patterns — always apply

Before adding a new file, component, workflow, or convention in this repository or any repository
it routes to: read and apply
[`finding-existing-patterns/SKILL.md`](../skills/finding-existing-patterns/SKILL.md) — find the
existing instances, conform to them, and treat "there is no existing pattern" as a claim you must
prove, not a default you may assume.

## Forbidden

- Introducing a new shape "just this once" without running the skill's search first.
- Concluding a pattern doesn't exist from a search that skipped gitignored or vendored trees.
